# iOS Outgoing packageClassList HARD LOCK

**HARD LOCK (2026-07-28).** Full doc: `docs/dibay-call-ios-outgoing-package-classlist-hard-lock.md`.

## Why

`npx cap sync ios` overwrites `ios/App/App/capacitor.config.json` `packageClassList` with node_modules plugins only. Dropping `NativeCallServicePlugin` breaks **iOS outgoing** (`Error loading plugin NativeCallService`) while **incoming** CallKit/VoIP can still work.

Regression: `95e8100bc`. Restore: `a8cc203ec`.

## Required (Call outgoing only)

- `NativeCallServicePlugin`
- `DibayVoipCallPlugin`
- `DibayCallPipPlugin`

Merge SSOT (full App-target list including Auth/Delivery): `scripts/patch-ios-capacitor-package-class-list.mjs`.
Call subset export: `IOS_CALL_OUTGOING_PACKAGE_CLASSES`.

Auth launcher registration is **not** owned by this rule — see `docs/auth-ios-native-oauth-launcher-contract.md`.

## DO NOT (without explicit user approval)

- Remove the Call plugins above from `packageClassList`
- Run bare `npx cap sync ios` and commit without running the patch
- Change `cap:sync:ios` to omit the patch step
- “Fix” outgoing by web/Vercel-only redeploy when the plugin is missing from the installed App.app
- Embed `NativeOAuthLauncherPlugin` / Auth registration into this Call HARD LOCK

## After every iOS sync

```bash
npm run cap:sync:ios
# or: npx cap sync ios && node scripts/patch-ios-capacitor-package-class-list.mjs
npm run verify:ios-call-package-classlist-contract
```
